    "narration_segments": [
      {
        "artifact_id": "narration_segment_1",
        "stage_id": 1,
        "component_id": 1,
        "ssml": "<speak>Welcome to subtraction with borrowing! In this lesson, we will learn how to subtract big numbers by borrowing from our neighbour.</speak>",
        "timing_map": {
          "start_time": 0,
          "end_time": 10000
        },
        "highlight_map": {
          "subtraction": "<emphasis level='strong'>subtraction</emphasis>",
          "borrowing": "<emphasis level='strong'>borrowing</emphasis>"
        },
        "pronunciation_overrides": {
          "neighbour": "<say-as interpret-as='name'>neighbour</say-as>"
        }
      },
      {
        "artifact_id": "narration_segment_2",
        "stage_id": 2,
        "component_id": 3,
        "ssml": "<speak>Let's look at an example. If we have 45 apples in a basket and we give 27 apples to our friend, how many apples are left in the basket? We can subtract 27 from 45, but it's a bit tricky because 45 is much bigger than 27. That's where borrowing comes in.</speak>",
        "timing_map": {
          "start_time": 10000,
          "end_time": 20000
        },
        "highlight_map": {
          "27": "<emphasis level='strong'>27</emphasis>",
          "45": "<emphasis level='strong'>45</emphasis>"
        },
        "pronunciation_overrides": {
          "apples": "<say-as interpret-as='unit'>apples</say-as>"
        }
      },
      {
        "artifact_id": "narration_segment_3",
        "stage_id": 3,
        "component_id": 3,
        "ssml": "<speak>To solve this problem, we need to borrow some apples from our neighbour. Let's say we borrow 10 apples from our neighbour. Now we have 55 apples in total. We can subtract 27 from 55, which is easy. We have 28 apples left.</speak>",
        "timing_map": {
          "start_time": 20000,
          "end_time": 30000
        },
        "highlight_map": {
          "10": "<emphasis level='strong'>10</emphasis>",
          "55": "<emphasis level='strong'>55</emphasis>"
        },
        "pronunciation_overrides": {
          "neighbour": "<say-as interpret-as='name'>neighbour</say-as>"
        }
      },
      {
        "artifact_id": "narration_segment_4",
        "stage_id": 4,
        "component_id": 3,
        "ssml": "<speak>But wait, we borrowed 10 apples from our neighbour! So, we need to give them back. Let's subtract 10 from 28. We have 18 apples left. That's the correct answer!</speak>",
        "timing_map": {
          "start_time": 30000,
          "end_time": 40000
        },
        "highlight_map": {
          "10": "<emphasis level='strong'>10</emphasis>",
          "28": "<emphasis level='strong'>28</emphasis>"
        },
        "pronunciation_overrides": {
          "apples": "<say-as interpret-as='unit'>apples</say-as>"
        }
      },
      {
        "artifact_id": "narration_segment_5",
        "stage_id": 5,
        "component_id": 7,
        "ssml": "<speak>Now it's your turn to practice! Try solving some subtraction problems with borrowing. Remember to always borrow from your neighbour when you need to.</speak>",
        "timing_map": {
